      <div type="clause" n="3">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:Ine">Ine</ref> 3</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="3" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="90" ed="#liebermann"/>XLVII. Gif ðeowmon wyrce on Sunnandæg be his hlafordes hæse, sie<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Ine_3.lnote.oe.2"/> he frioh<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="6" target="#Ine_3.lnote.oe.6"/>, ⁊ se hlaford geselle<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="7" target="#Ine_3.lnote.oe.7"/> XXX scill.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#Ine_3.lnote.oe.3"/> to wite.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="3" corresp="#wit-bu"><pb n="90" ed="#liebermann"/>XLVII. Gif þeowmon werce on Sunnandæg be his hlafordes hæse, sie he freoh, ⁊ se hlaford ge . . . scill' . . .</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="3" corresp="#wit-h"><pb n="90" ed="#liebermann"/>XLVII. Gif ðeowmon<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#Ine_3.lnote.oe.4"/> wyrce on Sunnondæg be his hlafordes hæse, sy<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Ine_3.lnote.oe.1"/> he freoh, ⁊ se hlaford gesylle<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Ine_3.lnote.oe.1"/> XXX scll' to wite.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="3" corresp="#wit-b-no-prol"><pb n="91" ed="#liebermann"/>Gyf ðeowmon wyrce on Sunnandæg be his hlafordes hǽse, sy he freo, ⁊ se hlaford gesylle XXX scill' to wite.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="3" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="91" ed="#liebermann"/>Si seruus operetur die dominica per preceptum domini sui, sit liber, et dominus emendet triginta sol. ad witam.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#attenborough" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="36" ed="#attenborough"/>Gif ðeowmon wyrce on Sunnandæg be his hlafordes hæse, sie he frioh, ⁊ se hlaford geselle XXX scill. to wite.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="3" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="372" ed="#jurasinski-and-oliver"/>{XLVII} Gif ðeowman wyrce on Sunnandæg be his hlafordes hæse, sie he freoh, ⁊ se hlaford geselle XXX sciƚƚ to wite</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="91" ed="#liebermann"/>Wenn<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Ine_3.lnote.de.1"/> ein Sklav am Sonntag arbeitet auf seines Herrn Geheiss, werde er frei<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Ine_3.lnote.de.2"/>, und der Herr gebe 30 Schill. zur Strafe.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#Ine_3.lnote.de.3"/></ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">If a slave works on Sunday at his lord’s command, let him become free, and let the lord give 30 shillings as a fine.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#attenborough" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="37" ed="#attenborough"/>If a slave works on Sunday by his lord's command, he shall become free, and the lord shall pay a fine of 30 shillings.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#whitelock"><pb n="400" ed="#whitelock"/>If a slave works on Sunday at his master’s command, he is to be free, and the master is to pay 30 shillings as a fine.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="373" ed="#jurasinski-and-oliver"/>If a slave works on Sunday at his lord’s command, let him be free, and the lord must pay 30 shillings as fine.</ab>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#liebermann"><ref target="clause:IIEg_5">II Eg 5</ref>; <ref target="clause:IICn_45-3">II Cn 45.3</ref></note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="372"><label>compare</label> <ref target="clause:Wi_9">Wi 9–11</ref> <quote>Compare to Wihtred §8 [L9, 10, 11].</quote></note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="373"><label>similarly</label> <ref target="clause:Wi_9">Wi 9–11</ref> <quote>Wihtred §8 [L9, 10, 11] similarly prohibits working on Sunday.</quote></note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="391"><label>parallel</label> <ref target="clause:Wi_9">Wi 9</ref> <quote>Ine §3 discusses the penalty when a slave works on Sunday; the parallel in Wihtred §8 [L9] concerns an esne</quote></note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#wormald-mel" n="103"><ref target="clause:Wi_9">Wi 9–11</ref></note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="49"><ref target="clause:Wi_9">Wi 9–11</ref></note>
